      "result": "W",
      "result_description": "Wadebridge CC - 1st XI - Won",
      "result_applied_to": "36578",
      "match_notes": "Wadebridge ran out comfortable winners despite Adam Cocking's unbeaten hundred for Newquay at a surprisingly summery Egloshayle Park. The hosts gained an early upper hand via James Maycock's rapid 46, and never relinquished it all day, as Matt Jolliffe (38) and young Sam Richards (30) supported overseas debutant Cal Morse in his fluent 69. Joe Crane took 3-44 and Alex Bicknell 2-60 for Newquay as Wadebridge amassed an impressive 277-9. In reply, Newquay reached 57-1 but, after the dismissal of Ruben Clinton (22), fell away to 158-8 around Cocking's fine 112* before ending on 216-9. Alek Gill (3-37) and Stuart Parkyn (3-57) each took three wickets for the Swans.",
